{"id":"DRKS00041381","src":"drks","title":"Observational Cohort of the Study Network Critical Care","official":"","summary":"The SN CritCare observational cohort establishes an adaptive, nationwide research infrastructure that generates high-quality clinical data and biosamples to deepen scientific understanding of acute organ dysfunction and enable future evidence-based improvements in the care of critically ill patients aged 0 to 100+ years.","conditions":["Acute organ dysfunction in critically ill patients (0–100+ years)"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"Non-interventional study-related measures. These include the collection of clinical data, the use of routinely generated or protocol-defined biosamples, and module-specific follow-up processes for the organ-specific and cross-sectional modules."}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nEligible participants must meet all of the following overarching criteria:\r\n1. Age 0-100+ years, including neonates, infants, children, adolescents, adults and older adults\r\n2. Presence or clinical suspicion of acute organ dysfunction of at least one of the following organ systems:\r\no Brain\r\no Lung\r\no Heart\r\no Liver\r\no Kidney\r\n3. Admission to or treatment within a hospital setting providing critical care, including ICU and intermediate care (adult and paediatric units)\r\n4. Informed consent (Broad Consent by patient, legal guardian, or legally authorised representative) according to national ethical and legal requirements, including age-appropriate paediatric procedures\r\n5. Willingness to participate in prospective follow-up\nExclusion criteria:\nThe following overarching exclusion criteria apply:\r\n1. Situations that prohibit study participation according to ethical or legal requirements (e.g. prisoner)","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2026-08-19","pcd":"2030-07-31","upd":"2026-08-20","sponsor":"Universitätsklinikum Würzbur